# Committed audit artifacts are byte-exact evidence, not source. The pipeline
# writes them with newline="\n" on every platform and a determinism test asserts
# they are byte-identical across runs -- so git must not rewrite their line
# endings on checkout. Without this, a fresh clone on Windows gets a report.html
# whose bytes differ from the one the pipeline produces, and "byte-identical"
# stops being checkable by anyone who cloned.
examples/rsi2_nifty/audit_out/verdict.json   -text
examples/rsi2_nifty/audit_out/evidence.json  -text
examples/rsi2_nifty/audit_out/report.html    -text

# Parquet is binary. Git usually detects this, but the reference caches and the
# trial-series siblings are the evidence base; say it rather than rely on it.
*.parquet                                    binary
